    {
      "key": "[Must-fix] [P1; cluster 56] `skills/super-auto/SKILL.md:174`: honor task cleanup exits 3/4 and retained nested worktree/temp resources before allowing parent removal, and verify run-owned processes before deleting resources they may need. The phase-7 caller lists retained resources but still delegates parent deletion before its run-level stop. The cluster's independent Git fixture proves ordinary parent removal exits 0 and destroys a dirty child under ignored `.worktrees/`. Source evidence: cluster-56.md and `/tmp/ufz-review-cluster56-612ea0a7/.review-probes/`; the original finish instruction predates this diff, but this new safety contract remains uncovered. Add outer-finish coverage for retained descendants and unknown/surviving process outcomes.",
